{
  "content": "<h1><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Summary\">Summary</span></h1><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts Balance Business Count Off On Summary View\">The <strong>Summary</strong> tab shows the balances of various accounts, offering a swift overview of the financial wellbeing of your business.</p><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 inline-block pointer-events-none ltr:pr-8 rtl:pl-8\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-200 ltr:pl-8 rtl:pr-8\"><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"border-y ltr:border-l rtl:border-r border-neutral-300 bg-white p-4 flex gap-2 items-center\"><i class=\"fas fa-presentation text-neutral-400\"></i><span class=\"font-semibold text-sm text-[#428bca]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Summary\">Summary</span></span></div><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts And Assets Count Equity Expenses Income Is Liabilities On To ToDate\">This encompasses details on assets, liabilities, equity, income, and expenses, all organized into distinct accounts or categories for straightforward navigation.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Business Current On Rent To ToDate User Users\">It serves as a dashboard, allowing users to quickly check the current financial condition of their business.</p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Count\">Setting the Accounting Period</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action Balance Business By Is On Summary Transaction Transactions\">By default, the <em>Summary</em> tab shows balances for all entered transactions. This is appropriate if starting a new business on Manager.io.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Balance Count Current MoreThan On Rent Summary To ToDate\">However once you use Manager for more than one accounting period, you want to tailor your <em>Summary</em> screen so it shows balances for your current accounting period only.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And Business Edit On Other Summary To ToDate\">Click the <strong>Edit</strong> button to set the period for your <em>Summary</em> tab and other parameters relevant to your specific business situation.</p><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"mt-4 ms-4 pe-8 items-center bg-neutral-100 p-4 border-neutral-200 border-s border-t rounded-ss-lg flex gap-4 shadow-[inset_0px_1px_0px_#fff]\"><span class=\"text-base font-bold text-neutral-300 [text-shadow:_1px_1px_0px_#fff]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Summary\">Summary</span></span><span class=\"text-neutral-300 hover:text-neutral-400\"><i class=\"fas fa-square-question\" style=\"font-size: 16px\"></i></span><span class=\"bg-white text-neutral-700 border border-neutral-300 font-semibold rounded-md py-2 px-4 text-sm\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Edit\">Edit</span></span></div></div><p><span translate=\"true\" keywords=\"On\">For more information, see:</span> <a href=\"/guides/summary-form\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Summary\">Summary</span> &mdash; <span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Edit\">Edit</span></a></p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Custom Layout To ToDate\">Customizing the Layout</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts And ChartOfAccounts Count Group Layout On Summary To ToDate Total\">The layout of groups, accounts, and totals on the <em>Summary</em> tab can be adjusted through the <strong>Chart of Accounts</strong>.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Business Is On\">This feature helps in organizing your financial information in a way that best suits your business operations.</p><div class=\"flex pointer-events-none space-x-6 rtl:space-x-reverse items-center\"><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 inline-block ltr:pr-8 rtl:pl-8\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-200 ltr:pl-8 rtl:pr-8\"><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"border-y ltr:border-l rtl:border-r border-neutral-300 bg-white p-4 flex gap-2 items-center\"><i class=\"fas fa-cog text-neutral-400\"></i><span class=\"font-semibold text-sm text-[#428bca]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Settings\">Settings</span></span></div><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div></div></div><span class=\"rtl:hidden\"><i class=\"fas fa-circle-chevron-right text-lg text-neutral-300\"></i></span><span class=\"ltr:hidden\"><i class=\"fas fa-circle-chevron-left text-lg text-neutral-300\"></i></span><div class=\"border rounded inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"basis-72 flex items-center gap-2 p-4\"><i class=\"text-xl text-neutral-400 fas fa-fw fa-sitemap\"></i><span class=\"text-sm text-[#428bca]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ChartOfAccounts\">Chart of Accounts</span></span></div></div></div><p><span translate=\"true\" keywords=\"On\">For more information, see:</span> <a href=\"/guides/chart-of-accounts\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ChartOfAccounts\">Chart of Accounts</span></a></p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action On Transaction View\">Viewing Transaction Details</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts And Balance BalanceSheet Count Profit ProfitAndLossStatement ProfitAndLossStatementAccount Statement Summary\">The <em>Summary</em> tab shows balances for all your balance sheet and profit and loss statement accounts.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action Balance By On Summary To ToDate Transaction Transactions View\">However, you can also view all individual transactions making up your balances on the <em>Summary</em> tab by clicking the <strong>Transactions</strong> button in the bottom-right corner.</p><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 pb-4 inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 p-3 border-b\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-4\"><span class=\"border text-xs rounded py-1 px-2 bg-white border-neutral-300 text-neutral-400\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Transactions\">Transactions</span></span></div></div></div><p><span translate=\"true\" keywords=\"On\">For more information, see:</span> <a href=\"/guides/transactions\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Transactions\">Transactions</span></a></p>",
  "key": "summary-view"
}
